ated partitions, not identified real students.\",\n","        \"Primary benchmark uses 10 simulated clients; this is an algorithmic stress-test, not a claim of 10 real classrooms/devices.\",\n","        \"Extreme alpha=0.1 is treated as a stress condition; very small clients are allowed and handled explicitly.\",\n","        \"FGSM reuses cached clean IID model states; it does not retrain those models.\",\n","        \"Corrected DP v2 trains 60 matched non-private controls with the same Poisson sampling/update schedule; these controls are not copied from the older clean FL sweep.\",\n","    ]\n","}\n","with open(RESULTS_DIR / \"run_manifest_v3.json\", \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n","    json.dump(manifest, f, indent=2)\n","print(json.dumps(manifest, indent=2))\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"1d19d675","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.038341,"end_time":"2026-10-11T12:23:03.920358","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-11T12:23:03.882017","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["# Final research protocol\n","\n","**Primary federation size:** 10 simulated clients. There is no universal client-count threshold for a Q1-quality FL study; what matters is a justified, controlled client population and sensitivity to client-count assumptions. The primary benchmark therefore uses 10 clients, while an optional targeted 5-vs-10 sensitivity analysis is provided. Recent FL studies explicitly vary client counts because client count can affect accuracy, data fragmentation, and system cost. citeturn796241search0turn796241search2\n","\n","The ten clients are simulated partitions of the single public training set, not identified students/classes/devices. Results therefore describe algorithmic behavior under controlled partitions rather than subject-disjoint generalization or real deployment prevalence.\n","\n","Execution order:\n","1. Dataset audit, benchmark-validity audit, and centralized baselines.\n","2. Run the pre-flight validation cell.\n","3. Clean FL sweep — 20 seeds × (IID + five Dirichlet α values) × five aggregation methods = 600 runs. Every run checkpoints its result, final state, and round history.\n","4. Client unreliability sweep — 20 seeds × three original scenarios × five methods = 300 runs. Every run checkpoints its result.\n","5. Optional 5-vs-10 client sensitivity — targeted 120-run grid, OFF by default.\n","6. Blocked centralized sensitivity — five held-out blocks, checkpointed after each block.\n","7. Corrected DP privacy–utility sweep — 20 seeds × four finite ε × three aggregation methods = 240 private runs, plus 60 newly trained matched non-private controls. The controls use the same Poisson sampling/update schedule, with clipping and noise disabled; they are not copied from the older clean sweep.\n","8. FGSM — no retraining: reuse cached clean IID states for FedAvg/FedProx/CAFAD and evaluate ε_attack ∈ {0.05, 0.10, 0.15}. The attack gradient is computed once per model and reused across the three attack strengths.\n","9. Final statistics, figures, and manuscript tables — generated only from saved result files.\n","\n","Every long-running section writes atomic checkpoints to `/kaggle/working/attention_fl_v3_q1_10client_lrtuned_results/`. If a Kaggle session ends, rerun only the interrupted section; completed keys are skipped and no completed run is intentionally retrained.\n","\n","The code does not claim that ten simulated clients are equivalent to ten real classrooms or devices. Any final manuscript statement about scalability should be framed as controlled client-count sensitivity rather than deployment-scale validation.\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"f167e480","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.038369,"end_time":"2026-10-11T12:23:03.9971","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-11T12:23:03.958731","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## 19. Full Q1 benchmark execution and finalization\n","\n","The following cells replace the previous ad-hoc resumable cells. Checkpointing is built directly into each expensive experiment, so there is no separate bootstrap/resume section and no duplicate training for FGSM or convergence analysis."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":30,"id":"a95b5bbd","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-11T12:23:04.07691Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-11T12:23:04.076612Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-11T12:23:04.30698Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-11T12:23:04.306261Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.271739,"end_time":"2026-10-11T12:23:04.308374","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-11T12:23:04.036635","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["SMOKE TEST PASSED: {'accuracy': 0.7502001601281025, 'balanced_accuracy': np.float64(0.7458513097072419), 'f1': 0.7094972067039106, 'precision': 0.8037974683544303, 'recall': 0.635, 'mcc': np.float64(0.5062446812036279), 'auroc': np.float64(0.8050770416024654), 'method': 'FedAvg', 'seed': 0, 'final_cafad_weight_min': nan, 'final_cafad_weight_max': nan, 'final_cafad_masked_clients': nan}\n"]}],"source":["# 19A. Fast smoke test (small, non-paper run)\n","# Run this once after restarting a Kaggle kernel. It does not create manuscript results.\n","RUN_SMOKE_TEST = True\n","if RUN_SMOKE_TEST:\n","    smoke_parts = balanced_iid_partition(y_train, N_CLIENTS, seed=0)\n","    smoke_result, _, _ = run_federated(\n","        X_train, y_train, X_test, y_test, smoke_parts,\n","        method=\"FedAvg\", seed=0, rounds=2, local_epochs=1, batch_size=64\n","    )\n","    print(\"SMOKE TEST PASSED:\", smoke_result)\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":31,"id":"e98fe607","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-11T12:23:04.3917Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-11T12:23:04.391452Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-11T12:23:04.463362Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-11T12:23:04.462683Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.114647,"end_time":"2026-10-11T12:23:04.46466","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-11T12:23:04.350013","statu